2026-11-07T06:45:15.0504120Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0574350Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0576530Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0577950Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0578830Z 
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0579870Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0580870Z 
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0583390Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0584670Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0585500Z 
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0586040Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0586840Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0587470Z 
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0588070Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T06:45:15.0591020Z   $ sh ./install-nix
